{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And she seizes him by the privy parts.</b> By the limb of shame, and these are the testicles. And Onkelos translated: בבית בהתתיה, in the manner of את אודיתא ולא בהתתא. And Scripture punishes her and cuts off her hand — that is, the monetary value of her hand, and not her hand literally, for such is the tradition of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, that the matter is only monetary compensation; and it is like (Exodus 21:24) ״עין תחת עין״, which is not an actual eye but rather the monetary value of an eye. For she is not liable to have her hand cut off, since she did so only to save her husband from the hand of the one striking him. Nevertheless, she is liable to pay the monetary value of her hand, since she was brazen and sent her hand to seize hold of the place of nakedness."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:59.931470470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}